---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { asset, page } from '../lib/asset';
---

<Layout title="Agent channels — Codescribe" description="Talk to connected agent sessions from the Codescribe overlay. Choose a recipient, attach context, read the reply, and track delivery status." path="fleet">
  <Nav current="fleet" />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="section hero" aria-labelledby="fleet-title">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">CONNECTED AGENTS</p>
        <h1 id="fleet-title">Keep the conversation<br />in your workflow.</h1>
        <p class="sub">Address a connected agent by name or channel. Speak the request,
          attach the context, and read its answer in the overlay. Your existing
          agent session supplies the tools and working context.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section screens" aria-labelledby="screens-title">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">CHOOSE THE RECIPIENT</p>
        <h2 id="screens-title">One overlay for your conversations.</h2>
        <div class="screen-row">
          <div class="screen-copy">
            <h3>Named channels.</h3>
            <p>Assign a supported agent session to a numbered channel. The roster
              shows the recipient, listener status, and acknowledgments separately.
              Switch with your configured shortcut.</p>
          </div>
          <figure>
            <a class="screen-link" href={asset('shots/fleet-channels.webp')} aria-label="View the channel roster screenshot">
              <img src={asset('shots/fleet-channels.webp')} width="744" height="472" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                alt="Codescribe channel roster with named recipients, listener status, and acknowledgment status" />
            </a>
            <figcaption>Product screenshot. Names and channel assignments are user configured.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="screen-row">
          <div class="screen-copy">
            <h3>Shortcuts that fit your work.</h3>
            <p>Configure recording gestures and the channel modifier. Attach selected
              text while speaking, and choose whether completed dictation is pasted
              automatically or held for review.</p>
          </div>
          <figure>
            <a class="screen-link" href={asset('shots/fleet-hotkeys.webp')} aria-label="View the shortcuts settings screenshot">
              <img src={asset('shots/fleet-hotkeys.webp')} width="2366" height="1796" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                alt="Codescribe shortcuts settings for dictation, formatting, selection, agent channels, and paste behavior" />
            </a>
            <figcaption>Product screenshot. Labels and available controls may differ by version.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section circuit" aria-labelledby="loop-title">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE WORKFLOW</p>
        <h2 id="loop-title">Ask, follow up, keep the reply.</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><span class="n">01</span><p><strong>Connect.</strong> Install the agent bridge and attach a supported runtime session to a named channel.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">02</span><p><strong>Address.</strong> Choose the recipient and speak your request. You can include selected text or files as context.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">03</span><p><strong>Follow.</strong> Listener and delivery status help you distinguish a connected reader from an acknowledged message.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">04</span><p><strong>Reply.</strong> Read the agent's answer in the overlay. Spoken replies are optional and require a configured speech provider.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">05</span><p><strong>Continue.</strong> Keep the conversation in the agent's existing session. A delivery acknowledgment confirms receipt, not completion of the task.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section disc" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">SETUP AND DATA</p>
        <h2 id="setup-title">Use the services you choose.</h2>
        <p class="sub">Agent channels need an installed bridge, an attached runtime,
          and the credentials required by that runtime. Provider behavior determines
          when queued requests become available to a session; delivery time varies.</p>
        <p class="note">Requests and attached context go to the selected agent and its
          configured services. Remote AI and speech providers have their own data
          policies. <a href={page('privacy')}>Read how Codescribe handles your data</a>.</p>
        <p class="note">Connection instructions and the current supported runtime paths
          are documented in the <a href="https://github.com/vetcoders/codescribe/blob/main/skills/codescribe/SKILL.md">agent bridge guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section cta" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 id="cta-title">Bring voice to your next task.</h2>
        <a class="button" href={`${page('')}#install`}>Download Codescribe</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .section { padding: 96px 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .container { max-width: 1040px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .hero { padding: 130px 24px 96px; text-align: center; }
  h1 { font: 700 clamp(40px, 7vw, 72px) / 1.04 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.04em; color: var(--ink); margin: 18px 0; }
  h2 { font: 700 clamp(28px, 4.6vw, 44px) / 1.1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--ink); margin: 16px 0 28px; }
  h3 { font: 600 23px / 1.2 var(--font-display); color: var(--ink); }
  .sub, .note, .screen-copy p { font: 400 17px / 1.65 var(--font-display); color: var(--muted-2); }
  .hero .sub { max-width: 660px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .screen-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); align-items: center; gap: 56px; margin-top: 56px; }
  figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  .screen-link { display: block; border: 1px solid var(--stroke); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--bg-chip); }
  .screen-link img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 12px; font: 400 12px / 1.55 var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted-3); }
  .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 32px 0 0; }
  .steps li { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding: 20px 0; }
  .n { color: var(--terracotta); font: 500 13px var(--font-mono); }
  .steps p { margin: 0; font: 400 17px / 1.65 var(--font-display); color: var(--muted-2); }
  .steps strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .note a { text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .cta { text-align: center; }
  .button { display: inline-block; padding: 14px 26px; border-radius: 10px; background: var(--terracotta); color: var(--bg); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .section { padding: 72px 20px; }
    .hero { padding-top: 96px; }
    .screen-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .steps li { gap: 16px; }
  }
</style>
